qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OBSERVATION\nRCA complete. The five listed keys still let an empty env var override a non-empty file value. Scratch config set verify.require_environment='prod-env', verify.opcert_enforce_since='refs/tags/enforce', identity.enforce_since='refs/tags/identity', mcp.auth_required_scopes=['tickets:write','tickets:read'], and mcp.auth_jwt_expected_typ='at+jwt'. With the corresponding env vars present but empty, load_config resolved them as '', '', '', (), and ''.\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nThe mechanism is precedence plus permissive coercion. config._ordered_layers places env after project config; _config_sources.env_overrides treats mere presence of REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY> as an override even when the value is ''. _config_coercion._as_str returns str(v), so '' survives; _as_str_tuple splits '' and drops empty entries, yielding (). Consumers then interpret the empty result as disabled: verify_opcert uses cfg.verify.require_environment / opcert_enforce_since, verify_authorship uses cfg.identity.enforce_since, mcp_server passes required_scopes=list(... ) or None, and _mcp_auth only enforces expected_typ when the string is truthy.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nThe deterministic subprocess experiment used REBAR_CONFIG pointing at scratch config plus the five empty env vars. Evidence that would disprove the RCA would be ConfigError on empty env, or file values winning over empty env; neither occurred. Working comparison: the earlier boolean fix made _as_bool('') raise, but these string/tuple coercers still accept empty because empty is meaningful for some other keys.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nNeeds a small design choice, not a blanket coercer change: add per-key empty-env disposition (meaningful unset vs fault). For the protection-direction keys, fail closed when env is present empty; preserve documented empty defaults and consumer-side fail-closed checks for the already-safe keys.","timestamp":1788737927128029001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: follow standard practice of popular actively-maintained OSS projects for empty-env handling.","timestamp":1788761662268234001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Research summary: pydantic-settings documents env vars are parsed verbatim by default, including empty values, and offers an explicit env_ignore_empty option when callers want empty env vars ignored; pip documents environment variables override config files and warns empty strings are not equivalent to false (use no/false/0); Django deployment checks treat security-critical empty settings such as SECRET_KEY as invalid configuration. Decision applied: per-key policy, not blanket string coercion. Protection-direction keys with empty env overrides are faults; documented meaningful empty-env defaults remain accepted.","timestamp":1788765690691877001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and merged as Gerrit change 2746. Local verify passed (make verify with injected GIT_CONFIG variables unset); Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; submitted and fast-forwarded to merged ref 188dc1e8a0ebe27ece397012bcfe6df286a00a91.","timestamp":1788771280385115001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788587569215382001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5f0d5ff4-7cb7-4212-93ed-678030ebd211","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b2ff-2588-9bb7-4bd2"},{"link_uuid":"06391202-785c-41ad-a820-b78bc303aa33","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"611b-39ae-9376-47f8"},{"link_uuid":"389b0bdc-2c3b-4882-858e-b38943875b8f","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"b2ff-2588-9bb7-4bd2"}],"description":"## Context\n\nDiscovered while fixing `b2ff-2588-9bb7-4bd2` (change 2662), which closed the\nempty-string hole for the BOOLEAN class by making `_as_bool(\"\")` raise. That fix covers\nall 27 boolean config keys. AC5 of that bug asked for one pass over ALL config keys for\nother places `\"\"` resolves in an unsafe direction. This ticket carries the residue.\n\n## Post-fix sweep: `\"\"` through every coercer in `_config_sections._SECTIONS`\n\n67 of 104 keys now RAISE on `\"\"` — every bool, int, float, `_as_choice`, `_as_git_ref`,\n`_as_git_remote`, `_as_tracker_dir`. Those are done. 37 keys still accept it:\n\n- **27 `_as_str` keys -> `\"\"`**\n- **7 `_as_str_tuple` keys -> `()`**\n- **2 `_as_str_list` keys -> `[]`** (`code_health.scan_roots`, `include_extensions`)\n- **1 with a literal fallback** (`ticket.display_mode` -> `\"auto\"`)\n\n## Already safe — verified at the CONSUMER, not assumed\n\n- `mcp.http_allowed_hosts` / `http_allowed_origins`: an empty allowlist on a\n  non-loopback bind raises `McpStartupError` (`mcp_server.py` ~:518). Fails closed.\n- `mcp.auth_jwt_algorithms`: empty raises `AuthConfigError`\n  (`_mcp_auth.py:265`). Fails closed.\n- `jira.url` / `jira.user` / `jira.project` / `reconciler.base_url`: empty leaves the\n  integration unconfigured, so operations fail rather than proceed.\n- `reconciler.ca_bundle`: empty = system trust store, not a relaxation.\n\n## The residue that needs a disposition\n\nThese are keys where an env `\"\"` DEFEATS a file-set value in the protection direction.\nEach is a \"the operator configured a control, an expanded-to-nothing `${VAR}` removed\nit\" shape — the same mechanism as the original bug:\n\n- `verify.require_environment` — empty = op-cert environment binding OFF\n- `verify.opcert_enforce_since` — empty = no enforcement floor\n- `identity.enforce_since` — empty = no identity enforcement floor\n- `mcp.auth_required_scopes` — empty tuple -> `required_scopes=None`\n  (`mcp_server.py:577`), i.e. no scope requirement\n- `mcp.auth_jwt_expected_typ` — empty = no `typ` header check\n\n## Why this is NOT just \"make `_as_str` raise on empty\"\n\nFor several of these keys `\"\"` is the DOCUMENTED \"off\"/unset spelling and equals the\nbuilt-in default (`verify.require_environment` is empty in the committed `rebar.toml`),\nso a blanket raise would break the normal configuration. The boolean fix worked because\n`\"\"` was never a legitimate boolean; that argument does not transfer. The likely correct\nshape is a per-key declaration of whether empty is MEANINGFUL or a FAULT, applied in the\nenv layer rather than in the coercer.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Each of the five listed keys gets an explicit disposition: empty is meaningful\n      (documented) or empty is a fault (raises).\n- [x] Whatever mechanism is chosen is declarative per key, not a blanket rule over\n      `_as_str` / `_as_str_tuple` — a blanket rule breaks the documented empty defaults.\n- [x] A regression test drives the real resolver with `\"\"` against a file setting the\n      opposite for every key whose disposition is \"fault\", and pins the \"meaningful\"\n      ones as still accepting empty.\n- [x] The already-safe keys above keep their current consumer-side fail-closed\n      behaviour; the fix must not move that check out of the consumer.\n\n## Completion evidence 2026-09-07\n\n- The five protection-direction residue keys are explicitly declared in `_EMPTY_ENV_FAULT_KEYS` and now reject present-but-empty env overrides: `verify.require_environment`, `verify.opcert_enforce_since`, `identity.enforce_since`, `mcp.auth_required_scopes`, and `mcp.auth_jwt_expected_typ`.\n- The mechanism is per-key and env-layer-only (`source == \"env\"`); `_as_str` and `_as_str_tuple` remain permissive for file/default values.\n- Regression coverage in `tests/unit/test_config_empty_env_bool_b2ff.py` drives the real resolver against file values plus empty env overrides for each fault key, verifies non-empty env still overrides, and pins representative meaningful-empty policies (`ticket.default_assignee`, `ticket.display_mode`, `mcp.auth_proxy_scopes`).\n- The already-safe consumer-side checks are untouched; implementation changed only `_config_sections.py` env-layer coercion.\n- Verification: targeted `pytest tests/unit/test_config_empty_env_bool_b2ff.py -q` passed (100 tests); ruff and complexity check passed; full `make verify` passed; Gerrit change 2746 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and was submitted as 188dc1e8a0ebe27ece397012bcfe6df286a00a91.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"declare per-key empty-env fault policy for protection-direction string/tuple keys"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_empty_env_bool_b2ff.py","reason":"regression coverage for fault and meaningful empty-env dispositions"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","611b-39ae-9376-47f8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6a6000ea-6f35-4426-8068-83e9da87162d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ee17-de97-09bf-4df4","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Empty-string env overrides still defeat file-set values on five string/tuple config keys (the non-boolean residue of b2ff)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["aff304da-f734-4957-9291-58624b6b7a26","204f4ca9-0f12-4d44-98ae-789ead8a74d0","3b5af966-f668-4444-acf5-d506d4f2e741","56575ac4-ce03-47b5-88bb-a3b9bba8be07","829bc30e-f538-43e2-b98c-ceae0417035f","f1def33c-6321-4f55-9cfa-57c717d09e54","9bd2959f-45db-469f-b4d9-f7a4a131a557","06391202-785c-41ad-a820-b78bc303aa33","e9259e38-b474-4e36-93be-52bb26e1a599","a05ec23b-fb47-45d8-8b51-2fdb36dccd89","6a6000ea-6f35-4426-8068-83e9da87162d","f907442c-1c5d-45a4-b1d2-12aff8a3c80a","389b0bdc-2c3b-4882-858e-b38943875b8f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788774903624885001,"uuid":"33d4e01b-d4e5-42cd-977f-812cd990e084"}